@inject WizardState Wizard

<h2>Identity</h2>
<p>Pipelines authenticate through Azure DevOps <em>service connections</em> (Project settings → Service connections). Enter their names exactly as they appear there.</p>

<label for="azure-connection">Azure Resource Manager service connection</label>
<InputText id="azure-connection" @bind-Value="Wizard.AzureServiceConnection" class="form-control" placeholder="$(AZURE_SERVICE_CONNECTION)" />
<p class="hint">Used for Key Vault, infrastructure as code, App Service deployments and slot swaps. Prefer the literal name: some tasks cannot resolve a service connection from a variable.</p>

<label for="registry-connection">Docker registry service connection</label>
<InputText id="registry-connection" @bind-Value="Wizard.Definition.Artifact.ContainerRegistryConnection" class="form-control" placeholder="$(DOCKER_SERVICE_CONNECTION)" />

<div class="info-box">
    On-premises deployments run as the account of the Azure Pipelines agent on each server.
    Use a gMSA or a dedicated service account with rights to the deployment folders and to IIS or the Windows service,
    and keep any other credentials in a variable group or Key Vault (next step).
</div>
